# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CLIENT CONFIG — TEMPLATE ONLY. This file is COMMITTED; it documents which
# variables a build may supply, never their real values.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_, and it INLINES them at BUILD time.
# They are NOT read when the page loads, so a production value must be present
# when `npm run build` runs — setting it as a runtime config var does nothing.
#
#   local dev/demo → leave VITE_API_URL UNSET (see below)
#   production     → set VITE_API_URL in the build environment, then build
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where the CoDecep server is. Used by both the HTTP client (src/lib/api.js)
# and the Socket.io connection (src/socket.js) — they talk to the same server.
#
# UNSET is the local-dev contract: src/lib/config.js falls back to
# http://localhost:3001, which is exactly what the client used to hardcode. So
# `npm run dev` needs no env file at all and behaves as it always has.
#
# Set it ONLY for a deployed build, to the deployed server's origin, with no
# trailing path (a trailing slash is stripped for you):
#   VITE_API_URL=https://your-app.herokuapp.com
# VITE_API_URL=

# Per-request client debug traces (src/debug.js). Leave unset/off normally.
# VITE_DEBUG=true
